# =============================================================================
#  HFE.orch - Health Front End (AIH-HSP V1.1)
#  Workflow Description Language v0.3, AIF V3.0
#
#  One Controller, one Module (the Health Front End of one End User), which runs
#  until Stop. The User Agent of the Front End binds a device to every Port of the
#  Module's boundary, each to one Port, by Data Type and Port Number:
#
#    what the End User gives the Front End -
#      RegisterIn      the request to register with the Back End. The workflow joins the Back End's service first (the
#                      Controller is admitted by the Trust Authority the End User decided to trust); the request then goes
#                      to the Back End, and its answer comes back, between the Controllers
#      RequestIn       a request to be sent to the Back End (an upload, a processing)
#      HealthIn        the Health Data the End User acquired
#      LicenceIn       the Model Licence the End User provides for it
#
#    what the Back End gives the Front End -
#      (the request for the NN Model the Front End trained, and its answer, are External Ports:
#       the Controller of the Front End and that of the Back End exchange them, signed - no device)
#
#    what the Front End gives -
#      (a request to the Back End, and its answer, are External Ports like the registration: between the Controllers)
#      RegisterAnswerOut  to the End User: the answer of the Back End to the registration (the Tokens)
#      ResponseOut     to the End User: the answer to a request (the AIH Data of the Vault, when asked for it)
#      AraOut          to the End User: the ARA Data - the alert is the ARA Data, which carries the risk
#
#  WHO STARTS WHAT through this Front End: the End User's User Agent starts, with RequestIn, the upload of its AIH Data (Store) and a
#  processing of its own AIH Data (AIHDataProcessing, as its Tokens allow); the Health Front End of a Third-Party User asks for a
#  processing only (see TPU.orch). De-identification, anonymisation and audit are the End User's too, but the L2 of the Health Front
#  End has no Port for them (proposal in MKG/pending-changes.md): they still go through the Back End's User Agent (HfeUserAgent.DeIdentify, Audit).
#
#  Where the AIH Data is kept (the Secure Data Vault) is the End User's: the User
#  Agent asks the Controller to keep the storage there. It names no AIM; AIH Data
#  Processing keeps the AIH Data there through the storage API (there is no Storage AIM).
#  The Front End talks to the Back End only: never to another Front End.
# =============================================================================

workflow HFE over 1AIH-HFE-V1.1-I01

on Start:

    type    Vault (OSD-BTO-V1.5)
    ask Controller to start
    ask Controller to keep storage in "{Vault}"
    ask Controller to join "AIH-HBE" role FrontEnd

    stream  RegisterIn        (AIH-REG-V1.1:1) from device "RegisterIn"
    stream  RequestIn         (AIH-AHP-V1.1:1) from device "RequestIn"
    stream  HealthIn          (AIH-HLD-V1.1)   from device "HealthIn"
    stream  LicenceIn         (AIH-MDL-V1.1)   from device "LicenceIn"

    deliver RegisterAnswerOut (AIH-REG-V1.1:2) to device "RegisterAnswerOut"
    deliver ResponseOut       (AIH-AHP-V1.1:2) to device "ResponseOut"
    deliver AraOut            (AIH-ARD-V1.1)   to device "AraOut"

    loop until Stop:
        wait 1s

on Stop:
    ask Controller to stop
